---
/**
 * The array, written out.
 *
 * Generated from the selection rather than kept beside it, so it cannot fall
 * behind what is ticked — and so the page never shows an import line that
 * would not compile.
 *
 * A button and a `hidden`, not a `<details>`. Copy has to sit on the same line
 * as the disclosure, and inside a `<summary>` it is a control inside a control:
 * the click toggles the disclosure on its way past, and assistive technology
 * announces one thing that does two. Positioning it over the summary instead
 * meant a hard-coded right offset chosen to dodge the floating shortcuts
 * button, which is the kind of number that is wrong the moment anything near
 * it moves. A plain row with `aria-expanded` has neither problem.
 */
---

<div class="pg-code-drawer" data-static>
  <div class="pg-code-bar">
    <button
      type="button"
      class="pg-code-toggle"
      id="pg-code-toggle"
      aria-expanded="true"
      aria-controls="pg-code-body"
    >
      <span class="pg-code-caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      Your editor, as code
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="btn ghost small" id="pg-copy">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="pg-code" id="pg-code-body"><code class="mono" id="pg-code" /></pre>
</div>
